This is a static printed magazine page.

No camera movement.
No zoom.
No parallax.
No reframing.
No text animation.
No object animation.

The page title reads:

REST
Practices for Allowing Rest & Recovery

A resting figure lies centered on a bed.
A crescent moon glows softly inside a thought cloud above.
Stars are faint in a textured night sky.

Instruction panels read:

PAUSE – Stop adding input. No fixing. No optimizing.
DIM – Lower light, sound, and stimulation.
DREAM – Allow dreaming and deep imagery.
STAY – Remain at rest when the urge to act appears.

The effect band reads:
Allows the nervous system to downshift, restores baseline regulation, and reduces cognitive load.

The closing declaration reads:
NOTHING IS REQUIRED RIGHT NOW

Allowed animation:

– Extremely subtle floating dust particles
– Very faint star twinkle (minimal and slow)
– Gentle film grain breathing
– Soft luminance shimmer in crescent moon (barely perceptible)
– Slight ambient dark-to-warm tonal fluctuation

Not allowed:

– No body movement
– No breathing animation
– No panel motion
– No dramatic glow effects
– No parallax
– No mystical energy effects
– No lighting sweeps

The page should feel:

Deep.
Quiet.
Heavy but safe.
Like the body exhaling into night.

Duration: 6–8 seconds.
Seamless loop.
Analog and tactile.
